/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A multirotor has four or more rotors.
   - GSD (ground sample distance) is the ground size of one image pixel.
   - GSD is ground sample distance in metres per pixel; p is pixel pitch (pixel size) in metres; H is flying height above ground in metres; f is focal length in metres.
   - Overlap is the shared part of two photos.
   - With 80% along-track overlap, each new photo adds 20% new ground.
   - SfM (structure from motion) is a photogrammetric method that recovers 3D structure and camera positions from overlapping images.
   - Products: an orthomosaic is a seamless top-down map made from rectified images.
   - In India, the Directorate General of Civil Aviation (DGCA) regulates drones.
   - Uses: topographic mapping, construction monitoring, landslide and flood mapping, agriculture, and stockpile volumes.
*/
