/* book Worked example: Q: A drone camera has pixel size 2.4 µm, focal length 8.8 mm and an image of 5472 × 3648 pixels, flown with the short side along track. It flies at 120 m above ground. Find the GSD and the ground footprint. For a 3.0 km strip with 80 % along-track overlap, find the photo spacing and the number of images; with 70 % side overlap, find the spacing between strips.
   1. Convert units: p = 2.4 µm = 2.4 × 10⁻⁶ m; f = 8.8 mm = 0.0088 m; H = 120 m.
   2. GSD = p × H ÷ f = (2.4 × 10⁻⁶ × 120) ÷ 0.0088 = 0.0327 m = 3.27 cm per pixel.
   3. Footprint along track = 3648 × 0.03273 = 119.4 m; across track = 5472 × 0.03273 = 179.1 m.
   4. Along-track spacing = 119.4 × (1 − 0.80) = 119.4 × 0.20 = 23.9 m.
   5. Intervals in 3000 m = 3000 ÷ 23.88 = 125.6, rounded up to 126; images = 126 + 1 = 127.
   6. Strip spacing = 179.1 × (1 − 0.70) = 179.1 × 0.30 = 53.7 m.
   Answer: GSD 3.27 cm; footprint 119.4 m × 179.1 m; photos every 23.9 m, 127 images for the strip; strips 53.7 m apart. */
